{title: Weighed on the Scales}
{subtitle: Daniel 5:1–30}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 104}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [D7] | [G] | [Cm] [D7] |
| [G] | [G] | [G] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
King Belshazzar threw a party for a thousand of his [G7]lords
They drank the wine from the temple cups and laughed at [Cm]the holy things
They praised the gods of silver and the [Fm]gods of gold and stone
[G7]Then a hand came out of nowhere and the [Cm]laughter died alone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The fingers wrote upon the plaster by the lamp[G7]stand's light
The king's face turned to ashes and his knees [Cm]knocked in the night
No wise man in the city [Fm]could read the words or tell
So they [G7]called for the old exile, Daniel, [Cm]who knew God well
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
MENE, MENE, TEKEL, and PARSIN
[Fm]You have been weighed on the scales
And found too [G7]light
Weighed on the [Cm]scales and found too light
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
God has numbered the days of your kingdom
[Fm]And brought it to an end
[G7]Your kingdom has been divided
And [Cm]given to the Medes and Persians
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
MENE, MENE, TEKEL, and PARSIN
[Fm]You have been weighed on the scales
And found too [G7]light
Weighed on the [Cm]scales and found too light [Fm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
That very [G7]night [G]the king was [Cm]slain
Weighed on the [Fm]scales
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
